11.0.0 — ADM BWF export, Learn, MIDI Time Code

What is new since 10050. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds and tests; nothing
here is device-verified yet.
- "Export ADM BWF (immersive)...": every track to the master becomes a mono object at its pan
  position (pan automation moves it), returns and own-output tracks form a stereo bed; BW64 with
  chna and axml, 24-bit, 48 kHz. Read and rendered without warnings by the EBU ADM renderer
  (ear 2.1.0) offline; not tried in a DAW yet.
- Learn (Song menu, App, "Learn..."): eleven short chapters with the real menu paths, search.
- Timecode (MTC) under Connect: send at 24, 25, 29.97 drop-frame or 30 fps from a virtual source
  "Echoel Timecode" (start 01:00:00:00), or chase an incoming MTC. Off by default.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10050) — headphone spatial, pitch and texture, loop record, MIDI 2.0, light
cues, colour. Earlier: git history.
group.com.echoelmusic is in the app's entitlements since a14e1960a (F17, 2026-10-21); the import
of earlier songs has not been seen on a device yet.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (FOUNDER_INBOX rule 1: five per build; answer each yes or no):
1. Export ADM BWF from a song with three panned tracks and open it in a DAW with ADM import
   (Reaper with EAR, Nuendo, Fairlight). Are the objects where the pans were?
2. Song menu, App, "Learn...": search "slice", open the chapter. Do the menu paths match the app?
3. Timecode (MTC) on at 25 fps, QLab or Reaper listening to "Echoel Timecode". Does it count
   from 01:00:00:00 and jump on locate and stop?
4. Chase an MTC from QLab or Reaper. Does the song start, follow a jump and stop within a
   moment of the sender?
5. Open a song made before this build (with takes, cues, colour). Does everything come back?
